The release of a place that waits without time is its virtual time, not a span before it.
The kernel would look for it a span late, and the thread wait on the spent queue past the count it has time again;
a place with units that waits without time has its virtual time more than a span ahead of the clock and of the release.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: a lender's virtual time comes before the release
Report: a place's virtual time comes before the release
Witness: fuzz lend-own-time-comes

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -225,7 +225,7 @@ static bool has_time(const struct place *payer, const struct place *p, uint64_t
 /* The count a place's units give it time again at, with no request open: its virtual time less its span. */
 static uint64_t place_release(const struct place *p)
 {
-    return p->vt - place_span(p);
+    return p->vt;
